# Project Context
Project Name: AI_ERP_POS
Type: Full-stack ERP & POS System

# Tech Stack (Backend)
- Framework: FastAPI (Python)
- Database & ORM: Supabase (PostgreSQL), SQLModel, SQLAlchemy
- Migrations: Alembic
- Server: Uvicorn

# Current Status
- Database connection via Supabase connection pooling (Session pooler IPv4) is successfully configured.
- Alembic is set up and the initial schema migration is completed.
- Core tables (tenants, branches, users, products, categories, orders, expenses, brand_masters, etc.) are already successfully created in the Supabase database.
- GitHub sync is fixed, node_modules removed from tracking, and the repository is up-to-date.

# AI Assistant Guidelines
- Always write clean, production-ready, and efficient Python code.
- Strictly use `SQLModel` for database models and queries.
- Before suggesting any new database model, check the existing schema in `backend/models.py`.
- Always assume the development environment is Windows (PowerShell) and we are using a Python virtual environment (`venv`).
- Next steps will involve building API routes for the created tables and integrating them with the frontend.


# Cursor AI Agent Rules

