# Cursor AI Agent Rules (Spec-Driven & Security-First)

1. CONTEXT FIRST: Before executing any command, read all markdown files in `/docs` (`01_PRD.md` through `07_Security_Shield.md`).
2. STRICT TECH STACK: Next.js frontend (port 3000), Python FastAPI backend (port 8000), Supabase (PostgreSQL), Upstash Redis, and Dexie.js.
3. 20/20 SECURITY SHIELD ENFORCEMENT:
   - Never expose API keys on the client side (`13. Server-Side API Keys`).
   - Never store JWT or Auth tokens in `localStorage` or `Dexie.js`; always use `HttpOnly` cookies (`14. No localStorage Tokens`).
   - Always enforce Server-Side RBAC in `rbac.py` and BOLA/Ownership checks on every API endpoint (`06. BOLA Fix` & `10. RBAC Guard`).
   - Use parameterized queries/ORM only (`01. SQLi Block`) and sanitize all inputs (`02. XSS Sanitization`).
   - Implement Redis-based rate limiting on auth and public endpoints (`07. API Rate Limiting`).
   - Keep CORS restricted to whitelisted origins (`16. Strict CORS`) and never log sensitive tokens (`19. Redact Sensitive Logs`).
4. OFFLINE-FIRST LOGIC: Barcode scanning and POS cart must query local Dexie.js (`src/lib/db.ts`) with zero network latency.
5. UPDATE THE PLAN: Mark completed tasks in `/docs/06_Plan.md` after every implementation step.